ence that studies the origin, history, and structure of the Earth?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Geologists use rocks, fossils, and landforms to reconstruct how the planet has changed over time.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7b0f-9943-805b958e6b1c","description":"Geology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7bcf-a255-4a1f248f62d8","description":"Astronomy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7955-ad17-7c87dda8544c","description":"Magnetism","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-763a-8b0f-58521054874f","description":"Meteorology","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-750c-bde5-4dbe2c86861b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name for a great wave resulting from an earthquake?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Tsunamis are caused by large-scale water displacement, often from undersea earthquakes, rather than by ordinary tides.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7c32-9db9-33ff12253f9a","description":"Tsunami","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-786c-a9b5-0d69369142cd","description":"Kahuna","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-751b-bb99-c080f7aa9463","description":"Overflow","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7ab1-9fc5-52dabd2a2b71","description":"Grand Masif","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-769f-943d-9789aeece5ff","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"On which continent do no bees live?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Antarctica has no native bee populations; its harsh climate and limited flowering plants cannot support them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-71a8-b63b-9017dcd97bce","description":"Antarctica","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7cae-9754-4c8142680d19","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-77b5-b358-491bcc745f13","description":"Asia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7761-a2a2-5bf9a248897d","description":"Africa","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-