"Cabbage","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-755e-91b7-6e714c577192","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of the following is not a planet?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The Moon is Earth\'s natural satellite, orbiting Earth rather than the Sun directly.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-752c-aa7a-7de3383ee39d","description":"The Moon","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-730a-8273-61e5c8561990","description":"Mars","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7b0b-a4b0-5128b4cfc50a","description":"Jupiter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7c62-a3e3-6dcca8451ac1","description":"Mercury","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-70c3-9e0e-ffb7555d497d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What does the word \"chlorophyll\" mean in its Greek origin?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Chlorophyll absorbs light for photosynthesis; its Greek name combines chloros, meaning \u201cgreen,\u201d and phyllon, meaning \u201cleaf.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7afb-b2d0-9bd260fc0035","description":"Green leaf","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-79d4-8093-1bc2ad1dd053","description":"Brown bark","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-757e-90f3-f2174d8b36ce","description":"Red flower","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7681-b757-5cdfe2dd9407","description":"Juicy fruit","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-72ca-b994-cf0cf72602b5","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"When chopping an onion, which glands in the eyes produce tears?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Onion vapors irritate the eyes and trigger reflex tear production by the lachrymal glands.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7fdd-8c59-4784851d8781","description":"The lachrymal glands","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7e99-816f-c975b24742b4","description":"The salivary glands","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7f83-b285-304856eba4e7","