ve in sub-Saharan Africa, with a small remnant in Iran.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7889-b5c6-8eaa749b984f","description":"Africa","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-703f-85c1-836e4ec3b2cf","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7456-98f2-95fd197f578b","description":"Europe","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7784-aa8e-27152b874bfa","description":"South America","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-73ee-b556-8144c0c8aba1","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What are the first digits of pi?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"3.14 is a common approximation of pi, whose decimal digits continue forever without repeating.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-738f-b56a-9348bf16aec1","description":"3.14","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7f56-977e-58cf6150dc3c","description":"3.41","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-731e-9b49-076a9831b195","description":"4.31","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-76f7-b776-cacdff974dca","description":"1.34","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7a95-a54b-5f9bbf9fc000","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is used as a disinfectant in swimming pools?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Chlorine helps kill harmful microbes in pool water. The familiar strong pool odor often comes from chloramines formed when chlorine reacts with contaminants.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7198-b73e-2c340b0fc713","description":"Chlorine","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7cfe-9c65-63ab420b21a5","description":"Sulfur","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-75c5-ae25-da89793e3b96","description":"Carbon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7c18-9903-d89975f73381","description":"Cobalt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-75f2-b52d-41f4c24b1801","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is used by submarines to observe the surface from a concealed position?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A periscope redirects light, letting someone see over an obstruction while staying concealed.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7d85-8f98-e6a81a256984","description":"Periscope","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7562-accb-5d0070de2795","description":"Episcope","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-761f-ae6c-bf33192e6a35","description":"Stroboscope","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7fff-9e24-493a0253328c","description":"Stethoscope","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-744b-a833-228b42d6c729","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What do herbivores eat?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Herbivores eat plants, and many have teeth or digestive systems suited to grazing or browsing.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7e23-afca-11ec821d63fb","description":"Plants","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7e01-bf56-022efac4359a","description":"Beetles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-76ff-a4ed-60c76ceab66c","description":"Snails","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-72cc-84d2-1a8b0a189669","description":"Fish","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7520-a438-88c95819c80a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"The cranium, which encloses the brain, is part of which larger bony structure?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The skull includes both the cranium, which protects the brain, and the facial bones.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-78c7-859a-032ff819e427","description":"Skull","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-72f0-9d83-e6def71e52dc","description":"Pelvis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7942-aa36-579008f4c3e4","description":"Spine","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7d35-bac5-126a3e14bcbf","description":"Ribcage","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7dbd-9cd1-cf52faa00f06","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who developed the theory of evolution by natural selection?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Charles Darwin set out natural selection in On the Origin of Species (1859), developed after his voyage on HMS Beagle.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7b14-b046-e1f6a86e2686","description":"Charles Darwin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7b30-a2c4-cbcea7bbf650","description":"Albert Einstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7df9-81a4-5358c027728e","description":"Isaac Newton","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7a42-bac0-7804d944d252","description":"Galileo Galilei","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7bb1-9623-1404b85632af","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which term refers to objects or lines that are side by side and will never intersect?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Parallel lines stay the same distance apart; perpendicular lines meet at a right angle, while convergent lines move toward one another.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7fa1-88fe-3db24763968b","description":"Parallel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7647-bb41-d411e96c2baf","description":"Perpendicular","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7d81-9b77-9da98ff75fd2","description":"Diagonal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7477-97f8-8c6adb4155ec","description":"Convergent","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-71e4-ba89-11b50186b3f6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Marine iguanas, saltwater crocodiles, sea snakes and sea turtles all belong to which class of animals?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Reptiles are air-breathing vertebrates with scales. Sea turtles must surface for air, while marine iguanas can hold their breath underwater.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-79dc-9c18-d5e29fa4822c","description":"Reptiles","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7b97-a647-d8c3471b8cc2","description":"Mammals","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-76da-832d-02369a5be997","description":"Amphibians","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-71ec-91a3-54fc1c045d4d","description":"Fish","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7228-800c-c261854ee616","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What would you call a baby owl?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"An owlet is a young owl; the ending -let often marks something small or young, as in piglet.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7c23-a438-f84c04978794","description":"An Owlet","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7f75-88cb-11c63408487a","description":"A Caterpillar","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7aa3-8672-67754286776a","description":"A Codling","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7ac5-b175-6206964bd9e7","description":"A Colt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-773c-8d31-aba35ff995d7","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A young butterfly is known as what?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A caterpillar is a butterfly\'s larval stage; after growing, it forms a chrysalis and later emerges as an adult.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7878-a412-366770edb332","description":"A Caterpillar","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7485-bb77-bd4ec54b25bb","description":"A Codling","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7762-a415-6479f3982af1","description":"A Chick","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7f23-b545-3af0d21c32d4","description":"A Spiderling","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-77b0-a161-598bb86eaffd","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What type of tree do both dates and coconuts come from?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Date palms and coconut palms are different members of the palm family, which also includes many ornamental and oil-producing plants.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-777e-aea1-be4064301b21","description":"Palm tree","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7c1c-b3e7-d27f6c2b6b2f","description":"Maple tree","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-730c-9990-16601f53c59f","description":"Birch tree","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7848-bb8b-3a6d646b35a2","description":"Fir tree","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-756b-8d7f-65faee322e04","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which fruit carries its achenes (ovaries with seed) on the outside?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The red flesh is an enlarged flower receptacle; each achene is a tiny dry fruit containing a seed.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7747-a902-2db0c81f3bd7","description":"Strawberry","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7ca5-bc69-f4abee3886d0","description":"Apple","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-733f-b2f6-012127732b98","description":"Grape","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7267-aafb-c861cf3ce0ee","description":"Banana","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7081-9958-35574ddd5eb7","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of lions?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A pride typically includes related females, their cubs, and one or more adult males.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-701e-93b3-1df4d6f351b8","description":"A pride","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7e55-bc7c-263a4dbc83bd","description":"A muster","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-71df-9537-7af2b4bfed41","description":"A clowder","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-72a2-887a-7044a9a93f9f","description":"A shrewdness","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7017-a921-1be89d52488d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the largest planet in the solar system?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Jupiter is a gas giant, and its Great Red Spot is larger than Earth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7cf3-b376-56587e486c15","description":"Jupiter","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-79d9-9cb8-c3eb17f990c0","description":"Saturn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-734f-b689-6a1d9dc41330","description":"Earth","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7a41-a448-ee742a0e05ee","description":"Uranus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-70f8-87af-3b8bcdf2448b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the process by which both milk and blood can become semisolid?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Clotting occurs as fibrin forms a mesh in blood; in milk, proteins gather into curds, as in cheese-making.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-732a-9909-4c94e0ed3576","description":"Clotting","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7d45-a9ec-b41d28dffa62","description":"Pasteurization","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7b-7f68-9e0d-49ba80d04f5d","description":"Filtration","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7290-bc2c-d2c633376992","description":"Distillation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-730c-b901-103e3fe9d538","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the term for a mineral that contains metal?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"An ore contains enough valuable material to make extraction worthwhile; not every metal-bearing rock qualifies.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-71ef-9bad-8ab97b09d6c8","description":"Ore","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7959-8266-37afd9c531f8","description":"Peat","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-790a-80c4-7de6f65eb75e","description":"Stone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7ee5-98c3-8708c32fa969","description":"Cement","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-75b5-857f-e07f90b9b3d5","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A female deer is known as what?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A doe is also an adult female rabbit; an adult male deer is called a buck.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-77e6-826b-4665a8fd2781","description":"A Doe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7421-8e33-17b42ebc20e5","description":"A Pen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7f6a-a999-d6f2688ec9a5","description":"A Mare","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7c92-a0a3-e3c539deb1b7","description":"A Nanny","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7e3d-be06-89278cedecff","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What kind of organism is a leech?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A leech is a parasite because it feeds on a host; many species use suckers to attach to animals.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-795a-a727-2a9bf57590eb","description":"Parasite","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7efd-a929-3ef34b5bc8ed","description":"Herbivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-77a3-bb00-ce1017df440a","description":"Omnivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-78f0-8342-5f37d629eeb0","description":"Decomposer","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7c3a-8361-f16b20ebdd58","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the largest snake?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Anacondas are generally considered the largest snakes by weight, though reticulated pythons can grow longer.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7adf-b9dc-f675322a27d2","description":"Anaconda","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-792c-8112-0f1e29f9a05e","description":"Black mamba","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7c72-ab05-26a7a9063919","description":"Rattlesnake","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-76db-98d0-067f7ad6a7a6","description":"King cobra","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7bf3-8f0a-d0da6a95dc2d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What type of shape might be obtuse or isosceles?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A triangle\'s angles total 180 degrees; obtuse describes one angle greater than 90 degrees, while isosceles means two sides are equal.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7c71-913b-ac0ecc4a461c","description":"A Triangle","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-74f4-80aa-9a1dc0313698","description":"A Square","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7e2f-b60a-2c9fc9d84602","description":"A Circle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7bf6-bc33-4172811c5122","description":"A Rectangle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-73b2-985b-b33272d04d43","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is made out of gravel, sand, cement and water?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Concrete hardens as cement reacts with water, binding the sand and gravel together.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7a2b-a564-448ad9c39c0c","description":"Concrete","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-723b-b939-53c93c6e66d5","description":"Porcelain","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-71ff-96fc-c89cb3696a30","description":"Gypsum","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7609-a777-460bfedcc2be","description":"Chalk","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7281-8aaf-653f64951d4a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many limbs does an octopus have?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"An octopus has 8 limbs, usually called arms. They contain no bones, which helps the animal squeeze through narrow spaces.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-77ba-8be2-22b254184c5d","description":"8","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-721c-b6b6-12acfd6d979c","description":"6","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-735b-beb6-a187226332d7","description":"10","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7da7-aec4-075b896505cd","description":"14","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7642-b865-4884cd3f4166","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"The chemistry of life centers around which element?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Carbon has four valence electrons, allowing it to form stable bonds with many elements and build the chains and rings found in biomolecules.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-a