},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-786c-bd8f-db7e36ccefec","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What force keeps the water in the oceans?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Gravity holds ocean water to Earth, while the Moon\'s gravity also helps create tides.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7920-8c22-bcba4f767765","description":"Gravity","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-73e5-bc5e-a3e104d9bd7f","description":"Friction","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7d86-b5bf-58e547d18733","description":"Magnetic force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7764-8d5c-aaf7051fd57e","description":"Air resistance","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7780-aaf7-e6a9e9844b62","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What was created with the big bang?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The Big Bang was the expansion of the early Universe, not an explosion into preexisting empty space.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7674-ab62-a30e79ae5340","description":"The Universe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7d75-a669-65c03c8080e0","description":"The Milky Way","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7f84-94b2-8a70bc1f8d76","description":"Andromeda","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-75ec-818a-d36be02a2667","description":"Infinity","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-794c-a176-1ecdb1d4f8e2","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A female horse is known as what?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A mare is an adult female horse; a young female horse is called a filly.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7dca-af2c-e13f8cd7156f","description":"A Mare","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7b52-928d-247e1a888507","description":"A Hen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7d8b-a23e-f2387800652a","description":"A Hembra","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7dbd-aef6-d09bd6fe9667","description":"A Jill","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-