":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7ce5-ac4b-2e15b86f515e","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Pediatrics is the branch of medicine that provides care for which of these groups?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Infants receive pediatric care, and pediatricians also treat patients through adolescence.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7fdd-be7c-8bd0b747d8e7","description":"Infants","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-747a-8a50-2c448aa124e1","description":"Elders","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7611-9a27-5d98806e9409","description":"Veterans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7333-9b22-e7e14223f3d9","description":"Women","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7d3a-8597-055c09e37f06","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the death of an entire species?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Extinction is global when no individuals of a species remain anywhere; disappearing from one region alone does not count.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7abb-9f29-eaad84c3ad87","description":"Extinction","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-79e8-9139-21e4c92d49bf","description":"Adaptation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7261-85f1-bd4d6bfd2fd2","description":"Evolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7208-89a5-de0ef6026e87","description":"Migration","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7f46-98ee-4b416edb001a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What does pH measure?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A pH of 7 is neutral; lower readings indicate greater acidity, while higher readings indicate greater alkalinity.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-75f8-adac-644b00a0d5a7","description":"Acidity and alkalinity","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7de7-9e1d-fc678ba821ed","description":"Temperature","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7a09-979f-c4e30c2b6fdf","description":"Density","correct_answer":false},{