","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7ef2-9a57-ac0b251c9c5e","description":"nutrition","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-73e0-8078-f6cede2072a2","description":"the signification and application of words","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7b91-86e5-70a17a48c8a3","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What acts as an exchange surface between mother and embryo?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The placenta attaches to the uterine wall, and the umbilical cord carries substances between it and the fetus; their blood supplies generally remain separate.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-78fe-bfc3-515953a93b98","description":"Placenta","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-792a-87f3-b3c05c41463b","description":"Ovaries","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-77e3-88a2-079a578e7483","description":"Cervix","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-721d-a4d0-871684023e1f","description":"Anus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-76b8-be4d-2b34e4f123f0","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What cell component is often used for personal identification?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"DNA carries inherited genetic information, and forensic profiling compares variable regions to help distinguish people.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-770d-9d87-1607341ef3e9","description":"DNA","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7937-ad4e-b79f57cb7a45","description":"Golgi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-774a-a032-ec425593f1b9","description":"Membrane","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7041-9d7c-9cc2d82194a9","description":"Cytoplasm","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-728f-a7dd-e86f0083d525","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is a decrease in hemoglobin or the number of red blood cells?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Anemia can cause weakness and shortness of breath because less oxygen reaches the body\'s ti