e},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-70fd-97e2-61e647d3f00a","description":"Ear","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-793b-87fa-dd66317c9862","description":"Stomach","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7e27-bfce-610bc5800f91","description":"Liver","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7f7b-916e-2bb09caedacc","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of the following particles does NOT carry electric charge?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Neutrinos are electrically neutral and come in electron, muon, and tau flavors; electrons, muons, and taus each carry electric charge.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7704-8548-10d1ac3050c1","description":"Neutrino","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7113-88c2-3e9f47d7af86","description":"Electron","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-72b0-b055-57e0e07d2464","description":"Muon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7309-904b-02b0ae5cb638","description":"Tau","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-763c-a1b2-ed346df56eb0","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What term is used for someone who studies physics?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A physicist investigates matter, energy, motion, and forces; a physician practices medicine.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-768b-847b-417dcec05a00","description":"Physicist","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7533-8375-5bbdb9cc7088","description":"Physician","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7207-ac9c-f435995bcfe2","description":"Physiatrist","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-79c5-b981-5a01bc9632bb","description":"Physicalist","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7873-8b38-fb59c2d50dd9","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What was the first name of the physicist Newton?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Isaac Newton also built an early practical reflecting telescope, which used mirrors rather than lenses to form an image.","alter