The 1s in 1010 occupy the eight and two places, which add to 10. Binary place values double from right to left.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7168-beb4-b4a0fc05e5a9","description":"10","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7fb5-b866-c15137743472","description":"8","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-70d2-97e5-6a8b2031d9b5","description":"12","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-78d6-93e7-aae35de413ff","description":"11","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7587-95f0-e03f19c08e7d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these snakes kills its prey by coiling around it and squeezing (a method called constriction)?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Pythons are nonvenomous constrictors that wrap around prey and squeeze; cobras, rattlesnakes, and puff adders rely on venom.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7771-bc2f-5911e22e89b3","description":"Python","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-754f-85c9-f86774cecef9","description":"Cobra","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-71ef-9b34-7a8dd436579e","description":"Rattlesnake","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7432-b2ac-54012c57ac62","description":"Puff adder","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7d26-9fb6-f991b923f155","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What can we measure with a protractor?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Angles are measured in degrees; a standard school protractor is marked from 0\u00b0 to 180\u00b0.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-79dd-bb79-bd6f8366611a","description":"Angles","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7d53-8fae-be3bd1a9e571","description":"Pressure","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-76b3-8992-7b8376ccd909","description":"Speed","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-729f-805d-a0e4412ed61f","description":"Force","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7292-af74-e849aecd8808","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","q