 Current Diode","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7fea-b197-0cb4c55aeda0","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the square root of 144?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A square root is a number that, multiplied by itself, gives the original value; 12 \u00d7 12 = 144.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7bca-8df5-dd22c2f9f0e5","description":"12","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7c13-b56c-92c7a46adedb","description":"11","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7c2f-b580-58fc83d53168","description":"13","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7a99-92e7-9e958cc08400","description":"14","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-741a-a1ce-76d023f01af1","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What instrument is made by rubbing a needle with a lodestone and floating it on a piece of wood in water?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A compass works because its magnetized needle aligns roughly north\u2013south with Earth\'s magnetic field.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7f3f-b3dc-ec475ef3155c","description":"Compass","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7882-9777-4f1663008c32","description":"Dynamo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-745f-9f33-eb3becc8ec47","description":"Geiger counter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7603-bc20-8971d4bb9210","description":"Chronometer","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7f85-b8d4-2a4f847fc821","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What silk structure do many insects use as a protective covering of the pupa?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A cocoon is a silk casing spun by many larvae; a chrysalis is the pupa itself, not its covering.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7da7-b473-ec60f6431e4e","description":"Cocoon","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7373-a6b0-994edc0a8d1a","description":"Chrysalis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7260-8735-e9bdfaf0c4ca","desc