3","description":"Stork","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7efb-ae66-1b410310ec4b","description":"Eagle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-797a-978b-ad78d62cc872","description":"Swan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-7c91-a382-a4b804c2793a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who is considered the inventor of the first commercially practical light bulb?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Thomas Edison developed a durable incandescent lamp and a practical electric-lighting system, helping make electric lighting commercially viable.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7c-70ad-976a-d3bef7b1241d","description":"Thomas Edison","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7c03-ada5-f1631a3e63e1","description":"Rudolf Diesel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7b6a-820b-ff77ab91b548","description":"John Fowler","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7a5c-8946-f46c34068c88","description":"Johannes Gutenberg","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-717f-82b1-62beac67e1f3","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many leaves does a shamrock have?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Three is the traditional leaf count; a four-leaf clover is a rare variation often treated as lucky.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7cfb-90cc-8206052431d6","description":"3","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7845-8d81-8dbeeef5b75d","description":"2","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7ab8-b4d4-17f34638b0a4","description":"4","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7c32-9d91-e09ab3cad28d","description":"5","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7e41-91fd-ef41079c7349","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is a doctor who specializes in the care of infants, children and teenagers called?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Pediatricians care for children\'s health broadly, while oncologists specialize in cancer treatment.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7422-8265-4d700151ccf6","description":"Pediatrician","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7469-a526-ab7005d84ade","description":"Physician","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7555-8acb-d5f5ab4587fb","description":"Oncologist","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-791e-8314-5218c0162bd2","description":"Gynecologist","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7718-807b-3b94faced193","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the outermost layer of our skin?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The epidermis continually sheds dead cells, while new cells rise from deeper layers to replace them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7e47-9057-0d0fc4c8afa0","description":"Epidermis","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7f70-b831-9eaa5a6165a3","description":"Dermis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-788d-8a10-78e4b97d4ded","description":"Cartilage","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-75e2-82f2-a9484c3535fa","description":"Ligament","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7d67-8efd-aaae70e05f14","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is astrology the study of?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Astrology uses birth charts and zodiac signs to make claims about personality and events; astronomy, by contrast, scientifically studies objects in space.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7bc4-85e1-2e093d4729e6","description":"The influences of celestial bodies on earthly affairs","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7f62-b388-acf88ad1a50e","description":"Friction at very small scale","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-70ac-ac20-b918281f819c","description":"The Sun","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-790e-9d06-1128b546cb75","description":"Men","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae7d-7dd9-b5a1-4f1bd6f373e6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What waste product is produced when we breathe?","diffi